  14: //! - **BA** (Built-in Administrators) - elevated operators
  15: //! - **IU** (Interactive) - interactive logon sessions (Session 1+)
  16: //!
  17: //! This replaces the prior **WD** (Everyone / World) grant, which contradicted
  18: //! T144 non-goals (multi-user World was listed as a security risk) and
  19: //! OPERATIONS prose ("interactive user").
  20: //!
  21: //! **Residual (R-MULTI / R-PIPE-IU):** On a multi-user machine, *any* interactive
  22: //! logon can open the pipe. Pipe messages still have no bearer (contrast HTTP).
  23: //! Single-owner desktops are the primary model; multi-user hosts accept residual
  24: //! risk documented in SECURITY-LIMITS.
